  "limits": [
    "The first baseline reported 4/7 passing because three negative tests accidentally caught the missing-helper assertion. That full output and source are preserved. Explicit helper-presence checks before rejection assertions produce the final 1/7 baseline with six intended missing-helper failures; no production behavior was relaxed.",
    "The seven new oracle cases and one maintained physical-send case are controlled Node checks. They do not execute the browser driver, IndexedDB, a validator or a financial journey.",
    "The browser driver gains a real UI proposal-save step, exact encrypted-record assertions and restoration/idle-unlock checks for the existing absent escrow. Its original 190 lines remain in order; original financial assertions and waits are unchanged.",
    "The proposal-aware wrapper admits only exact G35 records validated by the maintained decoder. Every remaining record reaches the unchanged strict legacy recovery/journal oracle. The original physical-send verifier remains byte-identical.",
    "The Node driver compilation emits and retains code and module hashes without evaluating generated code. It is not a configured-browser build or actual native acceptance.",
    "The earlier source verifier is reconstructed exactly by reversing the later additive UI-selector edit; both versions and their mapping are retained without rerunning either execution. Original execution receipts remain unchanged.",
    "Read-only setup path/glob failures are retained as a clearly labeled recovered diagnostic summary. They are not original validation logs and did not change source or test claims.",
    "The coordinator owns full repository qualification, current-source/current-target hosted acceptance and merge authorization. No remote publication, release, optional activation, new financial wait, validator setup, trust, key or endpoint was introduced by this companion."
